      "role": "user",
      "content": "i tried some pedialyte but he just spits it right back out or pukes it up immediately. the pharmacy is closed and i really dont wanna take him to the ER if it's something i can just fix here. i saw some old salt tablets in our first aid kit... would it be okay to crush those up in some water or juice to help him get his electrolytes back up faster? it seems like it would be more concentrated so it works better.",
